WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.442
AND means every connected condition must be true.

00:00:03.442 --> 00:00:07.412
In the example on this slide, a record must be active,

00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:12.227
the patient's age must be at least forty, and the severity must be High.

00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:17.247
If any one of those conditions is false, that row does not qualify.

00:00:17.247 --> 00:00:21.562
When you run the query, do not just look at the rows that remain.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:24.432
Also think about the rows that disappeared.

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:30.412
Maybe one patient is active and older than forty but has Medium severity.

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:35.187
That row fails because AND requires all three parts.

00:00:35.187 --> 00:00:39.412
A useful habit is to read the WHERE clause as a sentence.

00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:44.377
Say: I want patients who are active AND are at least forty AND have High severity.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:51.192
If the sentence sounds like all conditions are required at the same time, AND is the natural connector.

00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:53.612
This appears constantly in real projects.

00:00:53.612 --> 00:01:02.317
A university may select students who are currently enrolled AND have completed prerequisites AND have no

00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:04.442
registration hold.

00:01:04.442 --> 00:01:09.922
An e-commerce system may offer a promotion only to customers who are active AND belong to a certain

00:01:09.922 --> 00:01:12.157
region AND have a minimum purchase history.

00:01:12.157 --> 00:01:19.997
One important point: adding another AND condition usually narrows the result.

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:23.577
If you add a fourth requirement and your result becomes larger,

00:01:23.577 --> 00:01:26.382
that is a signal to inspect the logic.

00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:33.597
Before running a complex AND rule, predict at least one record that should qualify and one that should

00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:36.508
not. That simple habit makes debugging much easier.
